Title: Ilkley parking proposals 'written by Ebenezer Scrooge'
Date: 2025-07-14
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Ilkley Conservative councillor Andrew Loy', 'Text': 'Ilkley Conservative councillor Andrew Loy told a Bradford Council meeting that the changes could see people forced to pay to park outside church on Christmas Day.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 3, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 129}}, {'Speaker': 'Richard Downing', 'Text': 'It helps people shop locally and make visits to doctors and post offices. Having to pay to visit shops for a few items will make it inconvenient to shop locally – footfall will be down and people will be drawn to retail parks.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 11, 'StartChar': 19, 'EndChar': 243}}, {'Speaker': 'Richard Downing', 'Text': "Many residents will stop visiting the town's small businesses. Evening charges will deter people from visiting our theatres.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 12, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 111}}, {'Speaker': 'Councillor Alex Ross Shaw', 'Text': 'We recognise the number of responses to the petition. We do recognise the strength of feeling.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 14, 'StartChar': 53, 'EndChar': 141}}, {'Speaker': 'Councillor Alex Ross Shaw', 'Text': "We're looking at trying to find ways of managing the budget. Standardising parking charges is one way of doing this. I understand some people believe Ilkley is treated differently from the rest of the district, and I do want to push back on that.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 15, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 222}}, {'Speaker': 'Councillor Alex Ross Shaw', 'Text': "Charges have been changed or implemented right across the district. People often feel when a change comes in 'why my area?' but often the changes are taking place in similar ways right across the district.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 16, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 186}}, {'Speaker': 'Andrew Loy', 'Text': 'The charges will unfairly impact certain groups of people. They include the elderly, less mobile, parents dropping off children at school and parishioners of churches who rely on on-street parking to attend their local church services.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 18, 'StartChar': 10, 'EndChar': 208}}, {'Speaker': 'Andrew Loy', 'Text': 'How is it fair that they might face a parking fine for parking outside their church on Christmas Day?', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 19, 'StartChar': 1, 'EndChar': 82}}, {'Speaker': 'Andrew Loy', 'Text': "It's like Ebenezer Scrooge is writing the council's parking policy.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 20, 'StartChar': 1, 'EndChar': 63}}], 'Description': [{'Description': 'The petition on the Ilkley charges was presented by local resident Richard Downing, who said the removal of the free parking would be "immensely damaging" for local businesses.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 10, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 150}}, {'Description': 'He urged the council to scrap the proposed changes.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 13, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 46}}, {'Description': "He said there had been a considerable number of responses to the consultation, and that the final decision would be made by the council's executive.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 17, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 116}}, {'Description': 'Loy said charges would "deal a blow" to the town\'s restaurants, bars and venues like Ilkley Playhouse, Ilkley Cinema and King\'s Hall.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 18, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 88}}, {'Description': "Members voted for the petition to go to a future meeting of the council's executive.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 21, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 79}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': "A close up of an on street parking machine on a street with Yorkshire stone terraced buildings and business frontages. The machine has on it a label which says 'press green button for one hour free parking'"}]}
